eft" valign="top" charoff="50"><italic>romR</italic>&#x02237;<italic>nptII</italic>/P<sub><italic>nat</italic></sub>-<italic>romR-gfp</italic> (pSH1208)</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">This work</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">SA2272</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><italic>romR</italic>&#x02237;<italic>nptII</italic>/P<sub><italic>nat</italic></sub>-<italic>romR</italic><sup>&#x0002b;</sup> (pSH1206)</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">This work</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">SA2273</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">P<sub><italic>nat</italic></sub>-<italic>romR-gfp</italic> (pSH1208)</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">This work</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">SA2289</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x00394;<italic>pilA</italic>, <italic>romR</italic>&#x02237;<italic>nptII</italic>/P<sub><italic>nat</italic></sub>-<italic>romR-gfp</italic> (pSH1208)</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">This work</td></tr><tr><td colspan="3" align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><sup>a</sup>Plasmids mentioned in parentheses contain the <italic>romR</italic> or <italic>romR-gfp</italic> allele integrated at the chromosomal Mx8 attachment site. Structures of plasmids are shown in <xref ref-type="fig" rid="f1">Figure 1A</xref>. In P<italic><sub>nat</sub></italic> and P<italic><sub>pilA</sub></italic> constructs, the <italic>romR</italic> alleles were transcribed from the native <italic>romR</italic> promoter and the <italic>pilA</italic> promoter, respectively.</td></tr></tbody></table><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="7601877t2"/></alternatives></table-wrap></floats-group></article>